WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.120
How can you stop translating when speaking English?

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.040
Here's a question from Semsihan.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:12.560
How can I speak English
without translating from my language?

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.960
That was Semsihan's question,
but we want your questions too.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:24.600
You can email a question
to learningenglish@bbc.co.uk.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.000
But now, on to speaking
without translating. Let's go.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.200
Don't overthink.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.320
It's OK to make mistakes.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.000
If you're speaking
and you make a mistake,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.000
don't worry - and carry on speaking.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.240
When I moved to Spain, I was so
scared about making mistakes that I

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.440
just didn't speak. But then I decided
to stop worrying about it,

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.480
and I just spoke.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.800
And I realized that you learn
a lot more quickly,

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.800
and people are really kind and they
still understand what you're saying,

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.360
so just go for it.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.840
Think in English
and talk to yourself in English.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.320
It will make
the language seem more familiar

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.560
and it makes it part of your everyday life.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.640
Everyone thinks I'm talking on the phone,

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.720
but I'm actually just talking
to myself to practise my English.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.200
It's great! No one can tell.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.600
Associate new words and phrases
with language that you already know.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.520
This will help your brain to create links,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.520
and that will make
it easier to remember vocabulary

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.000
when you're speaking.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.760
Things at home you do with 'make'.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:32.200
OK, I make the bed, I make breakfast,
I make a mess, I make a cake.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:48.080
And it's better to learn phrases
instead of words, and use images too.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.160
Read books,

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.600
watch series,

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.240
listen to podcasts.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.280
Do things that you enjoy!

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.720
If you don't like classics,
then don't read classics in English!

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.480
That's all for now, but check below
for more on this topic.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.960
See you soon!

